  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements: one is labelled as Assertion (A) and the other is labelled as Reason (R).</p><p><strong>Assertion (A):</strong> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>-halocarboxylic acid on reaction with dil. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> gives good yield of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>-amino carboxylic acid whereas the yield of amines is very low when prepared from alkyl halides.</p><p><strong>Reason (R):</strong> Amino acids exist in zwitter ion form in aqueous medium.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>",
    "image": null
