    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/067f51f9-d05a-473e-98c7-db58c1bd4c4b-9896860.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 361px;\" /></p><p>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo></math>halocarboxylic acid react with dill NH<sub>3</sub> at faster than amines and amino acids exist in zwitter ion form in aqueous medium.</p><p>So, both (A) and (R) are correct and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).</p>",
